/// MISCOMPILE / TRAP (v-compiler-ml stress probe, 2026-07-16) — a String PARAMETER threaded through a
/// self-recursive loop AND used as a `String.concat` operand traps "out of bounds memory access" past ~3
/// iterations. `cdz check` CLEAN; `cdz compile` SUCCEEDS; RUNS → wasm trap at n>=4.
///
///   def build(s: String, n: Int64, acc: String) =
///     if n == 0 then acc else build(s, n - 1, String.concat(acc, s))
///   String.byte-len(build("x", n, ""))
///     n<=3 → correct (3); n>=4 → wasm trap: out of bounds memory access.
///
/// This is the STILL-LIVE-BINDING self-call family (cf. List.push/List.concat/Map.insert consumed-then-
/// read-again omitted-dup), on the STRING.CONCAT-with-a-threaded-param face — but here it TRAPS (OOB
/// memory access), not merely returns a wrong value: `s` is consumed by `String.concat` yet also passed
/// to the recursive `build(s, …)`, so the shared rope handle is freed/reused while still referenced, and
/// past a depth threshold the rope walk reads out of bounds.
///
/// SHARP DISCRIMINATORS (all verified 2026-07-16, cdz-run):
///   • Threshold is ITERATION COUNT, not byte length: a 1-char `s` traps at n>=4 (only 4 bytes) exactly as
///     a 2-char `s` does. So it's the number of chained runtime String.concat calls (rope depth), ~>=4.
///   • Concatenating a LITERAL each step — `String.concat(acc, "x")` (no threaded param) — WORKS to n=20+.
///   • NOT re-threading the param — concatenating a fresh helper result `String.concat(acc, one())` where
///     `def one() = "x"` — WORKS to n=8+.
///   • ONLY a String PARAMETER that is BOTH passed to the self-recursive call AND used as a concat operand
///     traps. Both operand positions fail: `String.concat(acc, s)` AND `String.concat(s, acc)`.
///   • 4 NESTED LITERAL concats const-fold (never run the runtime path) → correct; it is specifically the
///     RUNTIME self-recursive loop threading the param.
///   • CONTROL: the identical loop with `List.push(acc, 1)` (List, not String) works to n=10 — the List
///     still-live faces were fixed; the String.concat-threaded-param face is NOT.
///
/// IMPACT: HIGH for the port — a Cadenza-authored PRINTER/pretty-printer builds its output by threading
/// the string being appended (a separator, an indent unit, a token) through a recursive builder and
/// concatenating it each step; that traps past 3 pieces. Fix locus: the still-live-binding dup for a
/// `Core::BytesConcat`/String-concat operand that is a `Param`/`LocalRef` also passed to a self-recursive
/// call (backend/wasm/select.rs — same seam as the List.concat/push retain fixes, extended to the
/// String/Bytes concat op).
def build(s: String, n: Int64, acc: String) =
  if n == 0 then acc else build(s, n - 1, String.concat(acc, s))
def run(n: Int64) = String.byte-len(build("x", n, ""))
export { run }
